# modules/sast/rules/secrets.rules - docs/DESIGN.md §6.3 "secrets.rules" seed
# catalog: AWS keys, private-key headers, generic api_key=/password= literals,
# JWTs.  docs/FOUNDATION.md tension 9: every match here is exactly the kind of
# text the redaction pipeline (rules/redaction.rules) exists for.

id: SAST-SEC-AWS_AKID-01
title: Hardcoded AWS access key id
severity: critical
confidence: high
cwe: CWE-798
owasp: A07:2021
pattern: \b(AKIA|ASIA|AIDA|AROA|AIPA|ANPA|ANVA)[0-9A-Z]{16}\b
dialect: ere
context-deny: EXAMPLE|example|AKIAIOSFODNN7EXAMPLE|placeholder|XXXXXXXX
context-window: 0
tags: static
tags: quick
tags: compliance
remediation: Remove the key from source and rotate it immediately; a committed key must be
  treated as compromised even if the commit was reverted, because it remains in git history.
  Supply credentials through the instance role, the AWS profile, or the operator's secret store.
references: CWE-798
references: CIS-AWS-1.4
cis: 1.4

id: SAST-SEC-PRIVATE_KEY-01
title: Hardcoded private key
severity: critical
confidence: high
cwe: CWE-798
owasp: A07:2021
pattern: -----BEGIN ([A-Z]+ )?PRIVATE KEY-----
dialect: ere
tags: static
tags: quick
tags: compliance
remediation: Rotate the key pair and remove it from source; a private key committed to a
  repository must be treated as compromised, including in reverted commits.
  Load keys from a secret store or an instance-role-backed credential provider instead.
references: CWE-798

id: SAST-SEC-GENERIC_API_KEY-01
title: Hardcoded API key literal
severity: high
confidence: medium
cwe: CWE-798
owasp: A07:2021
pattern: (api[_-]?key|API[_-]?KEY)[[:space:]]*[:=][[:space:]]*["'][A-Za-z0-9_/+=-]{16,}["']
dialect: ere
context-deny: (EXAMPLE|example|CHANGEME|changeme|XXXXXXXX|xxxxxxxx|placeholder|dummy|your[_-]?api[_-]?key|TODO)
context-window: 0
tags: static
tags: quick
remediation: Remove the literal key from source and rotate it.
  Read the credential from an environment variable or a secret store at runtime instead
  of assigning it as a literal.
references: CWE-798

id: SAST-SEC-GENERIC_PASSWORD-01
title: Hardcoded password literal
severity: high
confidence: medium
cwe: CWE-798
owasp: A07:2021
pattern: (password|passwd|pwd)[[:space:]]*[:=][[:space:]]*["'][^"'[:space:]]{8,}["']
dialect: ere
context-deny: (CHANGEME|changeme|EXAMPLE|example|XXXXXXXX|xxxxxxxx|placeholder|dummy|\$\{)
context-window: 0
tags: static
remediation: Remove the literal password from source and rotate the credential.
  Read it from an environment variable or a secret store at runtime, never as a literal
  assignment in code.
references: CWE-798

id: SAST-SEC-JWT-01
title: Hardcoded JSON Web Token
severity: high
confidence: medium
cwe: CWE-798
owasp: A07:2021
pattern: eyJ[A-Za-z0-9_-]{5,}\.[A-Za-z0-9_-]{5,}\.[A-Za-z0-9_-]{5,}
dialect: ere
tags: static
remediation: Remove the token from source; a hardcoded JWT is a long-lived bearer credential
  and must be treated as compromised once committed.
  Mint tokens at runtime through the normal authentication flow instead.
references: CWE-798
